Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: allow supported audio containers in HLS children

The HLS-only format fence introduced during direct HTTP playback excludes
containers the pinned FFmpeg already handles. An actual-library fixture
decodes 96000 samples from each WAV/PCM, FLAC, Ogg/Opus and Matroska/PCM HLS
child without that exclusion; the previous list rejects all four before
decoding. Add these containers, not another demuxer or a retry policy.

Keep the list scoped to HLS child contexts by 0032. The protocol allowlist,
TLS verification, cancellation and read deadlines are unchanged. Tests also
check file rejection and HTTPS-root downgrade rejection; these are separate
boundaries, not a claim that every excluded format is intrinsically unsafe.
No attribution to an observed VRChat error is claimed.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
@@ -1001,7 +1001,7 @@
          * Constrain its child demuxers, not unrelated progressive containers. */
         if (av_dict_set_int( &options, "extension_picky", 0, 0 ) < 0) goto failed;
         if (av_dict_set( &options, "seg_format_options",
-                        "format_whitelist=mpegts,mov,aac,ac3,eac3,mp3,webvtt", 0 ) < 0) goto failed;
+                        "format_whitelist=mpegts,mov,aac,ac3,eac3,mp3,webvtt,wav,flac,ogg,matroska", 0 ) < 0) goto failed;
         demuxer->direct_url = TRUE;
         demuxer->require_avio_seek = TRUE;
         demuxer->io_timeout = HTTP_IO_TIMEOUT_US;
